{"name":"Pāua","hex":"#2a2551","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Pāua","blocks":[{"text":"Pāua is the Māori name given to four New Zealand species of large edible sea snails, marine gastropod molluscs which belong to the family Haliotidae. It is known in Australia and the United States as abalone, and in the United Kingdom as ormer shells. In New Zealand, these are known as pāua, which is both singular and plural. In New Zealand, the pāua's polished inner shell is widely utilised for jewellery and ornamentation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Haliotis_iris_LC0282.jpg/330px-Haliotis_iris_LC0282.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/P%C4%81ua","wikidata":"Q2658241"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a3/Three_abalone_p%C4%81ua_species_from_new_zealand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a3/Three_abalone_p%C4%81ua_species_from_new_zealand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"From left to right: black-foot pāua (Haliotis iris), yellow-foot pāua (Haliotis australis), virgin pāua (Haliotis virginea)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThree_abalone_p%C4%81ua_species_from_new_zealand.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Manawat%C4%81whi_p%C4%81ua_Haliotis_pirimoana_holotype_Te_Papa.jpg/500px-Manawat%C4%81whi_p%C4%81ua_Haliotis_pirimoana_holotype_Te_Papa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Manawat%C4%81whi_p%C4%81ua_Haliotis_pirimoana_holotype_Te_Papa.jpg/1280px-Manawat%C4%81whi_p%C4%81ua_Haliotis_pirimoana_holotype_Te_Papa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn